# Render round-R verify briefs (tag t) for every key: the workflow's verify prompt + ROUND-R NOTES.  Usage: python3 mkver.py R <number of rulings in adjudication-rR.md>
import json, os, subprocess, sys
SP = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
R = int(sys.argv[1]); P = R - 1; NR = int(sys.argv[2]) if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 0
KEYS = 'model kernel pipeline determinism rendering scope vol-V01-V02 vol-V03-V04 vol-V05-V06 vol-V07-V08 vol-V09-V10 vol-V11-V12 agree-fabric agree-layers agree-time agree-host agree-tools agree-proof edges-world edges-life'.split()
D = f'{SP}/rr{R}/verify'; os.makedirs(D, exist_ok=True)
for k in KEYS:
    json.dump({'key': k, 'round': R, 'tag': 't'}, open(f'{D}/{k}.json', 'w'))
    subprocess.run(['node', f'{SP}/prompts.mjs', 'verify', f'{D}/{k}.json', f'{D}/{k}.raw.txt'], check=True, capture_output=True)
    note = f"""

ROUND-{R} NOTES (orchestrator, 2026-10-01): (1) Your round-{P} findings are docs/validation/coherence/verify-{k}-r{P}t.md and results/coherence_verify-{k}-r{P}t.json. Repair round {R} sent every round-{P} finding (all twenty seats, merged by owner and id; the work files docs/validation/coherence/work/round{R}-work/<unit>.json) to its owner under the adjudicator's BINDING RULINGS, docs/validation/coherence/adjudication-r{R}.md ({NR} rulings, R{R}-01 – R{R}-{NR:02d}; its Part H gives every issue's disposition — FIX, FIX per a ruling, FIX amended, or MERGED into another id — its J141 grade, and the END lines one fix needed in a second unit); each owner wrote docs/validation/coherence/repair-r{R}-<unit>.md, which assemble-r{R} applied (docs/validation/coherence/assemble-r{R}.md: per unit what was applied, skipped or merged, every live file's sha256 before and after). The earlier adjudication files stay binding except where adjudication-r{R}.md supersedes an entry by name. (2) Re-check EVERY one of your round-{P} findings against the CURRENT live text — fixed, partly fixed, not fixed, fixed wrongly, or closed by a ruling (an issue MERGED into another closes when that one is fixed; a fix must match the ruling's text where Part H says \"per R{R}-nn\" or \"amended\", not the verifier's original wording) — including each END line's second end. Then re-check, whole subsection by subsection, everything a round-{R} block replaced, inserted or appended in your scope, for new problems the repair made. Ids outside both keep their earlier verdict. (3) THE BAR AND SEVERITY (owner, 2026-10-01, J141): the pass now stops when a full sweep finds zero blockers and zero majors (minors are still repaired; those left at the stop go to the builders' fix-list.md). Grade every finding by the SEVERITY STANDARD in the ground text above — blocker: cannot be built as written or a wrong result on a common path; major: two builders would build different behaviour; minor: nothing built or tested changes (wording, a citation, an id, a list or table omitting an id the rule itself names, a stale record, narration). When in doubt, ask what a build agent would do differently. (4) Owner rules first: file g items 102–126 and their canon routings decide; item 125 — the dossier is the only SettlementForge data input, the map code supplies the rest; item 126 (a2) — no map view on a phone at all (a phone clause still present is a defect; raise nothing that asks for one). (5) Keep the round-{P} issue id for a finding that persists; new findings take fresh ids with an r{R} marker. A finding ruled INVALID in any adjudication file is closed for good."""
    raw = open(f'{D}/{k}.raw.txt').read().rstrip('\n') + note
    open(f'{D}/{k}.full.txt', 'w').write(raw)
    r = subprocess.run(['python3', f'{SP}/finalize.py', f'coherence/verify-{k}-r{R}t', f'{D}/{k}.full.txt'], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)
    print(k, r.stdout.strip().split()[-1])
